From 6df4a6226b02ae4cf9ddfd01e8aa62793ae11e46 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Saulo Vallory <me@saulo.engineer>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 17:56:34 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] fix: shift numeric start/end once after parsing, not
 per-node during it

The per-node offsetAt() calls added in the previous commit shifted a
tag's start/end to absolute before onCloseTagEnd's locationAt(node)
read them back as if they were still fragment-relative, double-shifting
the resulting loc. Revert to fragment-relative start/end throughout
parsing (as before this patch), and shift every start/end once, in a
single walk, right after parsing finishes and before the top-level
ast/program start/end are set. loc (line/column) already comes out
correct at the source, via the patched positionAt/locationAt.

Added packages/compiler/test/parser-locations.test.js coverage for the
base-position option, including that MarkoTag/MarkoAttribute/the
tag-name StringLiteral carry no numeric start/end at all in this
compile mode (only loc) -- matching what mx's own fragment.ts already
documents -- while a nested Babel expression's loc.start.index is
where a numeric offset genuinely exists and must shift.

142 -> 147 passing (5 new tests), same 17 pre-existing failures as
before this patch and as unpatched main.
